        <mxCell id="4cd9yuj2vxOyTZg44lFt-8" value="THE DC MULYIVERSE OF THE BLEEDING EDGE CONTEXT:&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-d2f1cde9-7fff-e537-1039-b5eb2fca11b1&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The story opens with the Bleeding Edge, the crumbling barrier of the Multiverse. The Traveler awakens here, summoned by the Monitor. The Multiverse is destabilizing, timelines colliding, and the Source Wall’s collapse has unleashed Anti-Life corruption. From the very beginning, the player is presented with a binary choice: follow the Speed Force into Flashpoint’s broken timeline, or step through a Boom Tube into Apokolips’ cosmic war.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="102" y="257" width="550" height="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
